# Normalize EOL for all files that Git considers text files.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.pck filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ctex filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.tar.gz filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# .lmbake stays out of LFS on purpose. There are two of them, 510KB together,
# and they are the only LFS objects in the sparse checkout that the game
# actually needs - the rest is precompiled import output, which is an
# optimisation. Keeping half a megabyte of real assets behind an LFS budget is
# what stopped build #109 at step 2 with nothing else wrong.
*.lmbake binary
# The precompiled ASTC imports leave LFS for the same reason. They are the
# only LFS objects the build's sparse checkout still touches - the .pck and
# the .ctex tarball below live in lullaby_mod/original_pck/, which CI excludes
# - so as long as they are behind the filter, an exhausted LFS budget is a
# build outage. As plain git objects they cost repository size, which has no
# quota, instead of LFS bandwidth, which does.
#
# `binary` matters: the `* text=auto eol=lf` rule at the top of this file
# would otherwise try EOL normalisation on compressed texture data.
precompiled_astc_imports/*.res binary
